+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+/*
+ * Samsung S5K3T2: the front camera of the Xiaomi POCO X3 NFC (surya).
+ *
+ * WHY THIS SENSOR AND NOT THE REAR ONE
+ * -----------------------------------
+ * The 64 MP one at the back (IMX682) cannot be used with CAMSS, and not for lack of
+ * work: it is wired in C-PHY. This is measured in the factory calibration file
+ * of the phone itself, along two paths that agree:
+ *
+ *   laneAssign = 0x0210            tres lanes -> trios C-PHY
+ *   0x0114     = 0x02              three lanes, in the five mode tables
+ *
+ * CAMSS only supports D-PHY. The front one, in contrast, says laneAssign = 0x3210 and
+ * 0x0114 = 0x0300: four D-PHY lanes. See docs/CAMERA-04-rear-is-cphy.md.
+ *
+ * WHERE THE TABLES COME FROM
+ * -------------------------
+ * From the factory file of THIS phone and THIS module,
+ * com.qti.sensormodule.j20c_sunny_s5k3t2_front.bin, read with
+ * surya/camara/leer-sensormodule.py. They are not from another phone nor another
+ * vendor, so there is no PLL to recalculate.
+ *
+ * THE LINK ARITHMETIC, AND HOW IT WAS CHECKED
+ * ---------------------------------------------
+ * The PLL registers in the tables give, with INCK = 19.2 MHz:
+ *
+ *   vt_pix_clk = 19,2 / 3 (0x0304) * 185 (0x0306) / 1 (0x0302) / 7 (0x0300)
+ *              = 169,14 MHz
+ *   pixel_rate = vt_pix_clk * 4 pixels per cycle = 676.57 MHz
+ *   link_freq  = pixel_rate * 10 bits / (2 * 4 lanes) = 845,71 MHz
+ *
+ * The "4 pixels per cycle" is not assumed: it was calibrated against the sibling driver
+ * s5k3m5.c in this same tree, which declares 602.5 MHz and whose tables give
+ * exactly that figure with this same formula.
+ *
+ * And it checks out along a second path, the physical one: in the full mode there fit
+ * 5184 px x 10 bits / 4 lanes = 12960 bits per lane and line, which at
+ * 1691 Mbit/s take 7.66 us, within the 8.04 us the line lasts
+ * (5440 / 676.57 MHz). A 5% margin, which is exactly what is expected.
+ *
+ * Both modes come out at 30.1 fps, which is what is declared by whoever has already made
+ * this sensor capture on this same SoC (PR #59 of sm7150-mainline/linux).
+ *
+ * MODULE PARAMETERS, AND WHY THEY EXIST
+ * ---------------------------------------
+ * Two unknowns remain that cannot be resolved by reading, and this phone hangs
+ * on roughly one out of every four boots. So instead of
+ * spending a reboot per hypothesis, they go as parameters: they are tried with
+ * rmmod/insmod, without recompiling and without rebooting.
+ *
+ *   i2c_addr      the sensor address is not in the factory file
+ *                 (the only slaveAddr it carries is 0xa0, that is the EEPROM at
+ *                 0x50, the same trap that already cost time with the rear one).
+ *                 By default the driver SEARCHES for it by reading the ID.
+ *   mipi_switch   the front camera and the wide angle share CSIPHY1 through
+ *                 a MIPI switch, and which position is which is not known.
+ */
