+/*
+ * The previous 2 GiB/s are not enough: with the front sensor streaming and the
+ * CPU touching memory -which is exactly what happens when libcamera develops in
+ * software- the CSI-2 receiver runs out of FIFO after a few seconds and the
+ * pipeline stalls. It shows up as a lane overflow in
+ * CSID_CSI2_RX_IRQ_STATUS, followed by SMMU faults.
+ *
+ * The figure that fixes it is 4 GiB/s, and it is measured on the device by
+ * climbing the ladder one step at a time: at 2 and 3 it stalls, at 4 and 6 it runs clean. Raising
+ * the CAMNOC clock instead while leaving the old request in place changes nothing, so
+ * what is missing is the bus request, not the clock.
+ *
+ * And it is not the camera traffic: the sensor writes about 190 MB/s, twenty
+ * times less. What this buys is an operating point of the bus and of the DDR in
+ * which the receiver keeps being served even while memory is busy. That is why a
+ * modelo calculado a partir de resolucion x fotogramas x bits daria ~0,2 GB/s
+ * and it would make things worse.
+ *
+ * From sm7150-mainline/linux PR #59, measured on a Xiaomi Mi 9T (davinci) with
+ * this same SoC and this same sensor.
+ */
